  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers to pass east across the region early this \nmorning, then breezy conditions today.   \n\nMaturing surface low pressure centered over northern Wisconsin early \nthis morning, is associated with a deep trough and closed low over \nthe Great Lakes region today. As this system progresses eastward, \nthe surface low will move across the Great Lakes and into southern \nQuebec today and into Friday. Meanwhile, there is a surface cold \nfront currently lying across the Great Lakes this morning, where it \nwill sweep east across the region throughout the day today. Ahead of \nthe front, deep southerly flow originating from the Gulf and \nsouthern Atlantic has sent a plume of moisture into the region, \nsupporting widespread showers across the area this morning. Showers \nwill be on the lighter side, with rainfall amounts ranging between a \ntenth and a quarter of an inch across western New York, Genesee \nValley and the Finger Lakes region. Between a quarter and a half of \nan inch may be possible across north-central New York due to some \nupsloping off of the Tug Hill region.\n\nThese showers will begin to exit the region by mid morning today, \nthough a tight pressure gradient combined with a 30 to 40 knot low-\nlevel jet will support gusty winds across the region today. The \nstrongest winds will focus northeast of Lake Erie, where gusts of \nup to 35mph are expected.  \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Unsettled weather and cooler temperatures Friday \nthrough the weekend.\n\nThe aforementioned upper level trough and closed low from the \nprevious key message will move across the eastern Great Lakes region \nFriday through Saturday, where an additional cold front is progged \nto move across the region, supporting temperatures to trend cooler \nfor the end of the week and into the weekend. The cooler weather \ncombined with modest moisture will support daytime shower activity. \nAdditionally, cool wrap around moisture on the backside of the \nsurface low Friday night through Saturday night will support lake \nenhanced showers east/southeast of the lakes. Confidence in the \nprobability of precipitation forecast decreases Sunday and into the \nfollowing week as models diverge in the evolution of the mid-level \ntrough.",
